WEBVTT

NOTE
Amazona Verse pitch video (2:45.6). English subtitles of Juego/docs/pitch/VO.txt.
DRAFT: timings estimated from GUION.md; adjust to the final cut.

b01a
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.400
Her species is real.

b01b
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:09.400
In 2017, Hurricane María left El Yunque
without a single wild parrot.

b02a
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:15.800
Today there are more than 900, in forests and aviaries,
thanks to people who never gave up.

b02b
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.400
But our kids almost never see themselves in their games…

b02c
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:23.200
and schools are looking for science in Spanish that hooks them.

b03a
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.000
That's why we created Amazona Verse.

b03b
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:37.400
You are Vittata, a Boricua inventor, on an island inspired
by El Yunque, with trumpet trees and sierra palms.

b03c
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.600
She walks, flies, swims… and dives.
She marvels. She celebrates.

b03d
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.600
She dresses like us: a jíbaro straw hat…
and a cap with our flag.

b04a
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.800
Every mission teaches curriculum science.

b04b
00:00:51.000 --> 00:01:01.400
In “The Path of the Drop”, Vittata follows the water: up with the vapor to the cloud,
down with the rain to the river, and dives to the flood mark.

b04c
00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.600
First she predicts… then she checks.

b05
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:12.400
Every discovery goes into the Field Journal,
with a verified fact and its source.

b06a
00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:21.600
Teacher Mode includes a 45-minute lesson guide
and progress reports, with no personal data.

b06b
00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:25.200
In Spanish or English, with read-aloud.

b07a
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:33.200
In the nursery, your parrot grows with what you learn:
egg… baby… juvenile… adult.

b07b
00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:37.600
Just like the aviaries helping the species recover today.

b08a
00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.600
It runs in the browser, nothing to install,
designed for school Chromebooks.

b08b
00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:50.200
The engine is separate from the content: the next chapter,
or the next subject, builds on top.

b08c
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:55.000
And WebAssembly only where it helps, so it loads light.

b09a
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.800
We grow teacher to teacher:
free pilots in Puerto Rico;

b09b
00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:09.400
then the United States: nearly 99,000 public schools,
and almost 3 in 10 students are Hispanic.

b09c
00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:16.600
Chapter 1 is free. Schools pay an annual license;
families, optional digital clothing.

b09d
00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:20.000
No ads… and no loot boxes.

b10
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:28.000
We are looking for pilot schools, conservation partners and capital
to bring Amazona Verse to every classroom.

b11
00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:32.200
Because when our children learn to care for their island…

b12
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.600
the parrot flies again.
